-07-30","description":"Boise-based Micron Technology is no longer a trillion-dollar company, after several punishing days on Wall Street. The Boise-based chipmaker has seen several days of losses, with the stock dropping nearly ten percent Wednesday alone. The stock closed at $739 a share Wednesday, but kept sliding in after-hours trading. Micron’s total valuation stands at $834 billion […]"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},